<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proof of the Weighted SFT Loss</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In order to prove this theorem, we will first prove two lemmas, and then proceed to prove the main theorem. Our proof follows that of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ou et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, with the key difference that our <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> matrix incorporates varying masking rates <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, whereas <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ou et al., 2025</a>)</cite> assumes all masking rates are identical.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proof of Lemmas</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let the original response of the model be <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. At a given timestep <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, let the partially masked response be <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[M]</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the mask. <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{x_{t}^{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{x_{t}^{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the masking rate corresponding to the <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th token. The definition of <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{f}</annotation></semantics></math> can be found in Equation <a href="#S2.E6" title="In 2 Preliminaries: Continuous-Time Discrete Diffusion Model ‣ WeFT: Weighted Entropy-driven Fine-Tuning for dLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}^{i}=[M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}^{i}=[M]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{x^{\prime}}_{t}^{i}\neq[M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>x</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></mmultiscripts><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{x^{\prime}}_{t}^{i}\neq[M]</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{p_{t}(x_{t}^{1},\dots,{x^{\prime}}^{i}_{t},\dots,x_{t}^{d})}{p_{t}(x_{t}^{1},\dots,x^{i}_{t},\dots,x_{t}^{d})}=\frac{\exp(-\beta_{x_{t}^{i}}\,\bar{f}(t))}{1-\exp(-\beta_{x_{t}^{i}}\,\bar{f}(t))}\;p_{0}({x^{\prime}}_{t}^{i}\mid x_{t}^{\mathrm{unmasked}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>x</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></mmultiscripts><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>x</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></mmultiscripts><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>unmasked</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{p_{t}(x_{t}^{1},\dots,{x^{\prime}}^{i}_{t},\dots,x_{t}^{d})}{p_{t}(x_{t}^{1},\dots,x^{i}_{t},\dots,x_{t}^{d})}=\frac{\exp(-\beta_{x_{t}^{i}}\,\bar{f}(t))}{1-\exp(-\beta_{x_{t}^{i}}\,\bar{f}(t))}\;p_{0}({x^{\prime}}_{t}^{i}\mid x_{t}^{\mathrm{unmasked}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">On the other hand, if <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}^{i}\neq[M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}^{i}\neq[M]</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{p_{t}(x_{t}^{1},\dots,{x^{\prime}}^{i}_{t},\dots,x_{t}^{d})}{p_{t}(x_{t}^{1},\dots,x^{i}_{t},\dots,x_{t}^{d})}=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>x</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></mmultiscripts><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{p_{t}(x_{t}^{1},\dots,{x^{\prime}}^{i}_{t},\dots,x_{t}^{d})}{p_{t}(x_{t}^{1},\dots,x^{i}_{t},\dots,x_{t}^{d})}=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Intuitively, this theorem characterizes the exact transition probabilities during the training process. It also establishes a connection between the concrete score function and the clean data distribution via a scalar factor.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first calculate <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Based on the definition of <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can easily see that <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})=0</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}\neq x_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}\neq x_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}\neq[M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}\neq[M]</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now we divide the time interval <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,t)</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> intervals, namely <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,s_{1}),(s_{1},s_{2}),\cdots,(s_{n-1},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,s_{1}),(s_{1},s_{2}),\cdots,(s_{n-1},t)</annotation></semantics></math>. Here we denote <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0}=0,s_{n}=t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0}=0,s_{n}=t</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">then the total probability of <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t|0}(x_{t}=x_{0}|x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t|0}(x_{t}=x_{0}|x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\prod_{i=0}^{n-1}p_{s_{i+1}|s_{i}}(x_{s_{i+1}}=x_{s_{i}}|x_{s_{i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\prod_{i=0}^{n-1}p_{s_{i+1}|s_{i}}(x_{s_{i+1}}=x_{s_{i}}|x_{s_{i}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\prod_{i=0}^{n-1}(1+Q_{s_{i}}(x_{s_{i}},x_{s_{i}})(s_{i+1}-s_{i})+o(s_{i+1}-s_{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\prod_{i=0}^{n-1}(1+Q_{s_{i}}(x_{s_{i}},x_{s_{i}})(s_{i+1}-s_{i})+o(s_{i+1}-s_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\exp(\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}\ln(1+Q_{s_{i}}(x_{s_{i}},x_{s_{i}})(s_{i+1}-s_{i})+o(s_{i+1}-s_{i})))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\exp(\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}\ln(1+Q_{s_{i}}(x_{s_{i}},x_{s_{i}})(s_{i+1}-s_{i})+o(s_{i+1}-s_{i})))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\exp(\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(s_{i})Q(x_{s_{i}},x_{s_{i}})(s_{i+1}-s_{i})+o(s_{i+1}-s_{i})])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\exp(\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(s_{i})Q(x_{s_{i}},x_{s_{i}})(s_{i+1}-s_{i})+o(s_{i+1}-s_{i})])</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now we select the the appropriate <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{1},\dots,s_{n-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{1},\dots,s_{n-1}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\rightarrow+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\rightarrow+\infty</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max(s_{i+1}-s_{i})\rightarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max(s_{i+1}-s_{i})\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>, recalling the definition of integral, we obtain:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(s_{i})Q(x_{s_{i}},x_{s_{i}})(s_{i+1}-s_{i})+o(s_{i+1}-s_{i})])\rightarrow\exp(-\beta_{x_{0}}\bar{f}(t))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(s_{i})Q(x_{s_{i}},x_{s_{i}})(s_{i+1}-s_{i})+o(s_{i+1}-s_{i})])\rightarrow\exp(-\beta_{x_{0}}\bar{f}(t))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})=\left\{\begin{array}[]{ll}\exp(-\beta_{x_{0}}\bar{f}(t))&amp;\text{if }x_{t}=x_{0}\\
1-\exp(-\beta_{x_{0}}\bar{f}(t))&amp;\text{if }x_{t}=[M]\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{array}\right." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})=\left\{\begin{array}[]{ll}\exp(-\beta_{x_{0}}\bar{f}(t))&amp;\text{if }x_{t}=x_{0}\\
1-\exp(-\beta_{x_{0}}\bar{f}(t))&amp;\text{if }x_{t}=[M]\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{array}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, based on the above result, recall the independence of different dimensions in the diffusion process, we can get a stronger result:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose we have <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> in which the tokens <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1},a_{2},...,a_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1},a_{2},...,a_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> are masked and <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{1},b_{2},...,b_{n-k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{1},b_{2},...,b_{n-k}</annotation></semantics></math> are unmasked, then:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}(x_{t})=\prod_{i=1}^{k}(1-\exp(-\beta_{a_{i}}\bar{f}(t)))\prod_{j=1}^{n-k}\exp(-\beta_{b_{j}}\bar{f}(t))p_{0}(x_{t}^{\text{unmasked}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">unmasked</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}(x_{t})=\prod_{i=1}^{k}(1-\exp(-\beta_{a_{i}}\bar{f}(t)))\prod_{j=1}^{n-k}\exp(-\beta_{b_{j}}\bar{f}(t))p_{0}(x_{t}^{\text{unmasked}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Exploiting the independence across dimensions in the diffusion process, we may, without loss of generality, set <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}=i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}=i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}=k+i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}=k+i</annotation></semantics></math>. Equivalently, this corresponds to masking the first <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> tokens while leaving the remaining <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-k</annotation></semantics></math> tokens unmasked.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{t}([M][M]\dots[M]x_{t}^{k+1}x_{t}^{k+2}\dots x_{t}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{t}([M][M]\dots[M]x_{t}^{k+1}x_{t}^{k+2}\dots x_{t}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{x_{0}}p_{t|0}([M][M]\dots[M]x_{t}^{k+1}x_{t}^{k+2}\dots x_{t}^{n}|x_{0})p_{0}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{x_{0}}p_{t|0}([M][M]\dots[M]x_{t}^{k+1}x_{t}^{k+2}\dots x_{t}^{n}|x_{0})p_{0}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{x_{0}^{1}\dots x_{0}^{n}}p_{t|0}([M][M]\dots[M]x_{t}^{k+1}x_{t}^{k+2}\dots x_{t}^{n}|x_{0}^{1},x_{0}^{2},\dots x_{0}^{n})p_{0}(x_{0}^{1},\dots x_{0}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{x_{0}^{1}\dots x_{0}^{n}}p_{t|0}([M][M]\dots[M]x_{t}^{k+1}x_{t}^{k+2}\dots x_{t}^{n}|x_{0}^{1},x_{0}^{2},\dots x_{0}^{n})p_{0}(x_{0}^{1},\dots x_{0}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{x_{0}^{1}\dots x_{0}^{n}}\prod_{i=1}^{k}p^{k}_{t|0}([M]|x_{0}^{k})\prod_{i=k+1}^{n}p_{t|0}(x_{t}^{k}|x_{0}^{k})p_{0}(x_{0}^{1},\dots x_{0}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{x_{0}^{1}\dots x_{0}^{n}}\prod_{i=1}^{k}p^{k}_{t|0}([M]|x_{0}^{k})\prod_{i=k+1}^{n}p_{t|0}(x_{t}^{k}|x_{0}^{k})p_{0}(x_{0}^{1},\dots x_{0}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{x_{0}^{1}\dots x_{0}^{n}}\prod_{i=1}^{k}(1-\exp(-\beta_{i}\bar{f}(t)))\prod_{i=k+1}^{n}\exp(-\beta_{i}\bar{f}(t))p_{0}(x_{0}^{1},\dots x_{0}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{x_{0}^{1}\dots x_{0}^{n}}\prod_{i=1}^{k}(1-\exp(-\beta_{i}\bar{f}(t)))\prod_{i=k+1}^{n}\exp(-\beta_{i}\bar{f}(t))p_{0}(x_{0}^{1},\dots x_{0}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{x_{0}^{k+1}\dots x_{0}^{n}}\prod_{i=1}^{k}(1-\exp(-\beta_{i}\bar{f}(t)))\prod_{i=k+1}^{n}\exp(-\beta_{i}\bar{f}(t))p_{0}(x_{0}^{k+1},\dots x_{0}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{x_{0}^{k+1}\dots x_{0}^{n}}\prod_{i=1}^{k}(1-\exp(-\beta_{i}\bar{f}(t)))\prod_{i=k+1}^{n}\exp(-\beta_{i}\bar{f}(t))p_{0}(x_{0}^{k+1},\dots x_{0}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.SS1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}(x_{0}^{k+1},\dots,x_{0}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0}(x_{0}^{k+1},\dots,x_{0}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed as <math id="A1.SS1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}(x_{t}^{\text{unmasked}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>unmasked</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0}(x_{t}^{\text{unmasked}})</annotation></semantics></math>, the desired result follows.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now we append <math id="A1.SS1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to the above result and we obtain the result of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ A.1 Proof of Lemmas ‣ Appendix A Proof of the Weighted SFT Loss ‣ WeFT: Weighted Entropy-driven Fine-Tuning for dLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Proof of the Main Theorem</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3.2 Weighted SFT Loss Function Derivation ‣ 3 Method ‣ WeFT: Weighted Entropy-driven Fine-Tuning for dLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now we consider the Denoising Score Entropy, introduced in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lou et al. (2024)</a></cite>. DSE loss provides a principled training objective for diffusion models by measuring the discrepancy between the model score function and the true score of the perturbed data distribution.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">The DSE loss can be written as:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}\sum_{x_{t}^{\prime}\neq x_{t}}Q_{t}(x_{t}^{\prime},x_{t})(s_{\theta}(x,t)_{x_{t}^{\prime}}-\frac{p_{t|0}(x_{t}^{\prime}|x_{0})}{p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}\log s_{\theta}(x_{t},t)_{x_{t}^{\prime}}+C)dt" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}\sum_{x_{t}^{\prime}\neq x_{t}}Q_{t}(x_{t}^{\prime},x_{t})(s_{\theta}(x,t)_{x_{t}^{\prime}}-\frac{p_{t|0}(x_{t}^{\prime}|x_{0})}{p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}\log s_{\theta}(x_{t},t)_{x_{t}^{\prime}}+C)dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=K\!\left(\frac{p_{t|0}(x_{t}^{\prime}|x_{0})}{p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}\right),\quad K(a)=a\log a-a," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.751em;" width="0.751em"><mi>K</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=K\!\left(\frac{p_{t|0}(x_{t}^{\prime}|x_{0})}{p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}\right),\quad K(a)=a\log a-a,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Here <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant irrelevant to the loss.
The function <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\theta}(x_{t},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\theta}(x_{t},t)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes a score network used to estimate the ratio<math id="A1.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{p_{t}(x_{t}^{\prime})}{p_{t}(x_{t})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{p_{t}(x_{t}^{\prime})}{p_{t}(x_{t})}.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">In practice, we often estimate <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\theta}(x,t)_{x_{t}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\theta}(x,t)_{x_{t}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> using</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\theta}(x,t)_{x_{t}^{\prime}}\approx\frac{p_{t}(x_{t}^{1}\dots{x^{\prime}}^{i}_{t}\dots x_{t}^{d})}{p_{t}(x_{t}^{1}\dots x^{i}_{t}\dots x_{t}^{d})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>x</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\theta}(x,t)_{x_{t}^{\prime}}\approx\frac{p_{t}(x_{t}^{1}\dots{x^{\prime}}^{i}_{t}\dots x_{t}^{d})}{p_{t}(x_{t}^{1}\dots x^{i}_{t}\dots x_{t}^{d})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">We denote <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> as the reverse transition matrix corresponding to <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, the reverse process satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{Q}_{t}(x_{t},x_{t}^{\prime})=\left\{\begin{array}[]{ll}\frac{p_{t}(x_{t}^{\prime})}{p_{t}(x_{t})}Q_{t}(x_{t}^{\prime},x_{t})&amp;\text{if }x_{t}^{\prime}\neq x_{t}\\
-\sum_{k\neq x_{t}}\tilde{Q_{t}}(x_{t},k)&amp;\text{if }x_{t}^{\prime}=x_{t}\end{array}\right." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mo>∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{Q}_{t}(x_{t},x_{t}^{\prime})=\left\{\begin{array}[]{ll}\frac{p_{t}(x_{t}^{\prime})}{p_{t}(x_{t})}Q_{t}(x_{t}^{\prime},x_{t})&amp;\text{if }x_{t}^{\prime}\neq x_{t}\\
-\sum_{k\neq x_{t}}\tilde{Q_{t}}(x_{t},k)&amp;\text{if }x_{t}^{\prime}=x_{t}\end{array}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now we use Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ A.1 Proof of Lemmas ‣ Appendix A Proof of the Weighted SFT Loss ‣ WeFT: Weighted Entropy-driven Fine-Tuning for dLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and calculate the three parts of the loss separately:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using the fact that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum p_{0}({x^{\prime}}_{t}^{i}|x_{t}^{\text{unmasked}})=1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>x</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>unmasked</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum p_{0}({x^{\prime}}_{t}^{i}|x_{t}^{\text{unmasked}})=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">we obtain:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}\sum_{x_{t}^{\prime}\neq x_{t}}Q_{t}(x_{t}^{\prime},x_{t})s_{\theta}(x,t)_{x_{t}^{\prime}}dt=\int_{0}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}\sum_{x_{t}^{i}=[M]}\beta_{i}f(t)\frac{\exp(-\beta_{x_{t}^{i}}\bar{f}(t))}{1-\exp(-\beta_{x_{t}^{i}}\bar{f}(t))}dt" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}\sum_{x_{t}^{\prime}\neq x_{t}}Q_{t}(x_{t}^{\prime},x_{t})s_{\theta}(x,t)_{x_{t}^{\prime}}dt=\int_{0}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}\sum_{x_{t}^{i}=[M]}\beta_{i}f(t)\frac{\exp(-\beta_{x_{t}^{i}}\bar{f}(t))}{1-\exp(-\beta_{x_{t}^{i}}\bar{f}(t))}dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using the properties of <math id="A1.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\frac{p_{t|0}(x_{t}^{\prime}|x_{0})}{p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\frac{p_{t|0}(x_{t}^{\prime}|x_{0})}{p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}</annotation></semantics></math> we obtain:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{0}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}\sum_{x_{t}^{i}\neq x_{t}}Q_{t}(x_{t}^{\prime},x_{t})(-\frac{p_{t|0}(x_{t}^{\prime}|x_{0})}{p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}\log s_{\theta}(x_{t},t)_{x_{t}^{\prime}})dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{0}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}\sum_{x_{t}^{i}\neq x_{t}}Q_{t}(x_{t}^{\prime},x_{t})(-\frac{p_{t|0}(x_{t}^{\prime}|x_{0})}{p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}\log s_{\theta}(x_{t},t)_{x_{t}^{\prime}})dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}\sum_{x_{t}^{i}=[M],j\neq[M]}-f(t)\beta_{i}\mathbf{1}[x_{0}^{i}=j]\log s_{\theta}(x_{t},t)_{x_{t}^{\prime}}dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}\sum_{x_{t}^{i}=[M],j\neq[M]}-f(t)\beta_{i}\mathbf{1}[x_{0}^{i}=j]\log s_{\theta}(x_{t},t)_{x_{t}^{\prime}}dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recalling that <math id="A1.SS2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K(a)=a\log a-a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K(a)=a\log a-a</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>,
we can safely ignore the terms <math id="A1.SS2.p13.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{1}[x_{0}^{i}=j]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}[x_{0}^{i}=j]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq[M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq[M]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{0}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}\sum_{x_{t}^{\prime}\neq x_{t}}Q_{t}(x_{t}^{\prime},x_{t})K(\frac{p_{t|0}(x_{t}^{\prime}|x_{0})}{p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{0}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}\sum_{x_{t}^{\prime}\neq x_{t}}Q_{t}(x_{t}^{\prime},x_{t})K(\frac{p_{t|0}(x_{t}^{\prime}|x_{0})}{p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}\sum_{x_{t}^{i}=[M],j\neq[M]}\beta_{i}f(t)K(\frac{\exp(-\beta_{x_{t}^{i}}\bar{f}(t))}{1-\exp(-\beta_{x_{t}^{i}})\bar{f}(t))}\mathbf{1}[x_{0}^{i}=j])dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}\sum_{x_{t}^{i}=[M],j\neq[M]}\beta_{i}f(t)K(\frac{\exp(-\beta_{x_{t}^{i}}\bar{f}(t))}{1-\exp(-\beta_{x_{t}^{i}})\bar{f}(t))}\mathbf{1}[x_{0}^{i}=j])dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}\sum_{x_{t}^{i}=[M]}\beta_{i}f(t)\frac{\exp(-\beta_{x_{t}^{i}}\bar{f}(t))}{1-\exp(-\beta_{x_{t}^{i}})\bar{f}(t))}(\log\frac{\exp(-\beta_{x_{t}^{i}}\bar{f}(t))}{1-\exp(-\beta_{x_{t}^{i}})\bar{f}(t))}-1)dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}\sum_{x_{t}^{i}=[M]}\beta_{i}f(t)\frac{\exp(-\beta_{x_{t}^{i}}\bar{f}(t))}{1-\exp(-\beta_{x_{t}^{i}})\bar{f}(t))}(\log\frac{\exp(-\beta_{x_{t}^{i}}\bar{f}(t))}{1-\exp(-\beta_{x_{t}^{i}})\bar{f}(t))}-1)dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">By adding them all together, especially combining the first and third term, we get</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\int_{0}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}\sum_{x_{t}^{i}=[M]}-\frac{\beta_{i}f(t)\exp(-\beta_{i}\bar{f}(t))}{1-\exp(-\beta_{i}\bar{f}(t))}\log(\frac{\exp(-\beta_{i}\bar{f}(t))}{1-\exp(-\beta_{i}\bar{f}(t))}q_{\theta}(x_{0}^{i}|x_{t}^{\text{unmasked}}))dt" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>unmasked</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}\sum_{x_{t}^{i}=[M]}-\frac{\beta_{i}f(t)\exp(-\beta_{i}\bar{f}(t))}{1-\exp(-\beta_{i}\bar{f}(t))}\log(\frac{\exp(-\beta_{i}\bar{f}(t))}{1-\exp(-\beta_{i}\bar{f}(t))}q_{\theta}(x_{0}^{i}|x_{t}^{\text{unmasked}}))dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now we apply a change of variables. By defining</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}=1-\exp\!\big(-\beta_{x_{t}^{i}}\,\bar{f}(t)\big),dt_{i}=\beta_{x_{t}^{i}}f(t)\exp\!\big(-\beta_{x_{t}^{i}}\,\bar{f}(t)\big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}=1-\exp\!\big(-\beta_{x_{t}^{i}}\,\bar{f}(t)\big),dt_{i}=\beta_{x_{t}^{i}}f(t)\exp\!\big(-\beta_{x_{t}^{i}}\,\bar{f}(t)\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p17.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p17.2.1" class="ltx_text">the loss can be rewritten as:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{i}\int_{0}^{1}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}[-\frac{1}{t_{i}}\mathbf{1}[x_{t}^{i}=[\mathbf{M}]]\log(q_{\theta}(x_{0}^{i}|x_{t}^{\text{unmasked}})]dt_{i}+C" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝐌</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>unmasked</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}\int_{0}^{1}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}[-\frac{1}{t_{i}}\mathbf{1}[x_{t}^{i}=[\mathbf{M}]]\log(q_{\theta}(x_{0}^{i}|x_{t}^{\text{unmasked}})]dt_{i}+C</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p19" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">Here, <math id="A1.SS2.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the distribution in which <math id="A1.SS2.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is masked with probability <math id="A1.SS2.p19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p20" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}=1-\exp(-\beta_{x^{i}}\,\bar{f}(t))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}=1-\exp(-\beta_{x^{i}}\,\bar{f}(t)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p21" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose we have a reference value <math id="A1.SS2.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\text{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\text{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> and define</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1-\exp(-\beta_{\text{ref}}\,\bar{f}(t))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1-\exp(-\beta_{\text{ref}}\,\bar{f}(t)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p21.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p21.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then we can express <math id="A1.SS2.p21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> as</span></p>
<table id="A1.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}=1-(1-t)^{\frac{\beta_{x^{i}}}{\beta_{\text{ref}}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>β</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><msub><mi>β</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}=1-(1-t)^{\frac{\beta_{x^{i}}}{\beta_{\text{ref}}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text">In practice, one can sample <math id="A1.SS2.p22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and calculate <math id="A1.SS2.p22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> using the above formula.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Hyperparameters</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Training Hyperparameters</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our experiments are conducted with a learning rate of <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math> and a total of 20 training epochs.
We apply gradient accumulation with <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> steps and used an effective per-device training batch size of <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>.
To reduce memory cost, we employ LoRA with rank <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=128</annotation></semantics></math>, scaling factor <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>256</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=256</annotation></semantics></math>, and a dropout rate of <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.05</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.05</annotation></semantics></math>.
All hyperparameters, including model architecture, optimization, LoRA configuration, and training settings, are listed in Table <a href="#A2.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ B.1 Training Hyperparameters ‣ Appendix B Hyperparameters ‣ WeFT: Weighted Entropy-driven Fine-Tuning for dLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
